    aside(data-markdown).notes.
        Many violinists and luthiers report that a violin improves when it is played regularly. They say that the violin has "opened up".

section
    violin-book(
        title="A Treatise on the Structure and Preservation of the Violin"
        author="Jacob Augustus Otto"
        year="1860"
        page="47"
    )
        | "It may be received as an established truth, that an instrument acquires a
        | #[span.hl beautiful and mellow tone], not by age, but by
        | #[span.hl constant use]."

    aside(data-markdown).notes.
        This idea goes back at least 200 years. In the early 19th century, the German luthier and violinist Jacob Augustus Otto wrote in his "Treatise on the Structure and Preservation of the Violin":
        "It may be received as an established truth, that an instrument acquires a beautiful and mellow tone, not by age, but by constant use."

