    aside(data-markdown).notes.
        We wanted to revisit this question, with more complete measurements (both acoustic and perceptual) and additional hypotheses to explain what happens.
        When violinists think they have opened up a violin, either:
        1. the violin has changed
        2. the violinist's playing has changed (external adaptation)
        3. the violinist's perception has changed (internal adaptation)

