    aside(data-markdown).notes.
        The protocol was quite simple:
        1. a series of measurements on the instruments and the violinists is made at the start of the experiment. I will detail these measurements on the next slide.
        2. The Test Violinist plays the Test Violin until she considers it open. She alone decides how long this period lasts. Meanwhile, the Control Violins are not played, and the Control Violinists have no access to the instruments.
        3. At the end of this period, we make the series of measurements again.

        We actually made two series of measurements before the playing period, one week apart, to quantify the variability of our measurements before any effect could have taken place.

